fix(pip): Clear the second set's SSFX AO/IL for the lens pass, and correct the fog rationale

Review of the previous commit found the real mechanism, and the previous commit's rationale was
wrong in its details.

The SSFX AO and IL are cleared and computed inside the SVP guard in phase_combine, so the lens set
never computed them, but the combine reads both unconditionally. The clears belonged to the
"second set keeps its own buffers" rule, not to the phase gating, so the second set's maps kept
whatever they were created with - and the combine uses them as multipliers:
    hdiffuse.rgb *= ssfx_ao.Sample(...).www;
    hdiffuse *= lerp(1.0f, IL_sample * (30.0f * ssfx_il_setup.y), IL_sample);
A stale AO/IL map multiplied into the lens image is a flat dark mask over part of the aperture, and
it covers a larger share of the picture the more the optic magnifies, because the same map is
spread over a narrower view - which is exactly what the player reported. The clears now run for
every pass (the phases stay main pass only), and clearing to (0,0,0,1) is provably neutral for this
combine: the AO term is read from the map's ALPHA, which is 1 at that value, and the IL term is the
lerp factor itself, which at 0 selects the unmodified 1.0. This mirrors what the bloom already does
a few lines below.

The fog gating from the previous commit stands, but for a different reason than stated there. Its
geometry reconstruction is per pass and therefore correct for the lens (it reads
pos_decompression_params, uploaded for the active pass); what is wrong is that its blend consumes
the blur chain, which the lens pass deliberately does not generate. The comment now says that
instead of blaming the projection, and the rain refraction and the motion blur are gated for the
same reason: both consume main view buffers.